From 76e409b5be5370983e4517fa7bf2aef1564efc24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 11:26:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08089/11362] change_fidelity does not predict plannability; a
 bounded forward probe does

Scores 156 frozen induced engines (116 from the object-perception A/B over 20
games, 40 from the best-of-N over 5) on both sides of the question the A/B
raised and could not answer: does held-out change_fidelity make a plan more
likely to EXIST when plan_in_model walks the engine forward from the level root?

138 engines are analysable, 22 plannable, over 21 games.

  change_fidelity   AUC 0.6085, game-clustered 95% CI [0.381, 0.751]
                    within-game AUC 0.5688 over 11 informative games
                    point-biserial r 0.140 [-0.027, 0.300]
                    logistic slope 1.13, cluster CI [-3.68, 2.21]
                    with tn36 removed: AUC 0.532, CI [0.327, 0.698]

Every interval contains chance, in a design measured to detect an injected
AUC-0.75 association 97.5% of the time. So this is evidence of absence, not
absence of evidence. The object-perception effect is not, on this evidence, a
reason to flip anything.

What DOES predict it is structural, not accuracy-like: probe_depth_reached --
how deep a 600-call forward probe gets before the engine's own state graph
stops producing new states -- posts AUC 0.787, cluster CI [0.675, 0.859],
within-game 0.754, and survives family-wise correction over all 14 candidates
at FWER p = 0.0030. Do not wire it yet: it was selected from a family and needs
a prospective test on engines this run never saw.

Corrections to the framing this run was given:

* "All six perfect-fidelity candidates are unplannable" was a DEPTH-40
  artifact. At the shipped default of 80, three of the seven engines at
  change_fidelity >= 0.999 do plan. The run independently reproduces
  plan_max_depth_default's stated 2 -> 6 conversion, and all four gains are
  tn36.
* plan_in_model tests is_level_complete on successors only, never on the start
  grid, while the goal gate tests the root and rejects it. They therefore
  DISAGREE on goal-predicate-true-at-root: the gate vetoes, the planner returns
  a length-1 plan. 4 of the 22 plannable engines are that class. Production is
  safe because it runs the gate first.
* goal_satisfiable is barred from the rival ranking: the gate is the same
  bounded BFS from the same root, sharing the planner's depth resolver by
  design. Its AUC 0.909 is arithmetic, not a finding.
* 45 of 138 engines are inert at root and 0 of them plan, exactly as
  construction requires, so every structural predictor gets that separation for
  free. The live-only re-analysis is reported beside the pooled one.

Provenance: rebuilt objperc change_fidelity reproduces the frozen A/B on
114/114 cells; the rebuilt best-of-N split reproduces split.json's row counts
on 5/5 games; real root_grid and reconstructed window root agree on plan_found
on 31/31 engines. The estimator is checked against scipy's exact Mann-Whitney
on every run (40/40, and the extremal case lands exactly on the stated floor).

CPU only, no GPU, no generation. adversarial_verify 0-flagged.

